WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:16.999
I could react, Fritz raised his gun to his shoulder and fired at the shark.

2
00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:21.561
The monstrous fish disappeared under the water, and our sheep was safe.

3
00:00:21.581 --> 00:00:22.942
"Well done!"

4
00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:23.643
I cried.

5
00:00:24.403 --> 00:00:26.464
Fritz's eyes sparkled at my praise.

6
00:00:27.285 --> 00:00:30.607
He carefully watched the water for the shark, but it didn't reappear.

7
00:00:31.707 --> 00:00:36.229
With a breeze in our sail, we quickly reached shore where I released the animals.

8
00:00:38.991 --> 00:00:41.892
My wife and the three younger boys came running to meet us.

9
00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:46.054
They helped to collect the animals and unload supplies from our boat.

10
00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:50.596
We were hungry, but when we reached camp, there was no sign of supper.

11
00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:56.118
"Fritz and I can supply some ham," I volunteered, pointing to the supplies from the ship.

12
00:00:56.898 --> 00:00:57.759
My wife smiled.

13
00:00:57.779 --> 00:01:00.640
"Ernest, let's see if we can conjure up some eggs."

14
00:01:01.516 --> 00:01:02.437
"Where did you get these?"

15
00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:05.979
I asked as Ernest proudly set before me a dozen turtle eggs.

16
00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:11.823
"I'll tell you over supper when I describe how we spent our day," said my wife.

17
00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:15.565
Supper consisted of an omelet followed by ham and cheese.

18
00:01:16.746 --> 00:01:21.629
After I told the others about our adventures with the animals and shark, my wife began her story.

19
00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:28.254
"The sun beats down on this bare, rocky spot all day," she said.

20
00:01:28.274 --> 00:01:31.156
"And it's even hotter inside the tent.

21
00:01:31.984 --> 00:01:36.548
I decided that you and Fritz weren't the only ones who could do something for this family."

22
00:01:37.349 --> 00:01:40.512
So she and the boys had set out to find a cooler place to live.

23
00:01:41.373 --> 00:01:45.817
Accompanied by the two dogs, they'd crossed the stream and the field of tall grass.

24
00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:49.581
"We soon came to a grove of a dozen trees.

25
00:01:50.301 --> 00:01:54.445
I really can't describe how huge and strange they were," my wife continued.

26
00:01:54.465 --> 00:01:57.248
"Their roots arched above the ground."

27
00:01:58.152 --> 00:02:02.815
She told how Jack had scrambled up above the roots of one tree and measured its circumference with

28
00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:03.615
a piece of string.

29
00:02:03.635 --> 00:02:06.817
"I think it was eighteen yards around!"

30
00:02:07.197 --> 00:02:07.777
said Jack.

31
00:02:08.778 --> 00:02:14.221
The spot was shady and cool, and the longer they'd stayed there, the more my wife had liked

32
00:02:14.261 --> 00:02:21.805
it. "If only we could live among the branches of those grand, noble trees, I'd feel perfectly safe

33
00:02:21.885 --> 00:02:23.266
and happy," she said.

34
00:02:24.026 --> 00:02:27.388
She'd liked the place so much that she didn't feel the need to search anymore.

35
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.021
They'd returned home by way of the beach.

36
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:32.522
"That's where we found the eggs!"

37
00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:33.463
said Ernest.

38
00:02:33.483 --> 00:02:36.725
"Or I should say, the dogs found them."

39
00:02:37.525 --> 00:02:38.265
Everyone laughed.

40
00:02:39.786 --> 00:02:42.648
The boys went off to play while my wife and I continued to talk.

41
00:02:43.468 --> 00:02:48.511
"I hope you're in favor of packing everything up and taking us to live among my splendid trees,"

42
00:02:48.931 --> 00:02:49.411
said Mother.

43
00:02:49.431 --> 00:02:53.153
"So you want us to perch in these trees like birds?"

44
00:02:53.494 --> 00:02:53.834
I said.

45
00:02:53.854 --> 00:02:56.735
"If we had wings, it would be a wonderful idea."

46
00:02:58.184 --> 00:03:00.646
"My idea is not as silly as you think.

47
00:03:01.387 --> 00:03:04.309
A house among the branches would keep us safe from wild animals.

48
00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:07.152
And I've seen such a house in Switzerland.

49
00:03:07.572 --> 00:03:09.114
I climbed a staircase to reach it."

50
00:03:10.415 --> 00:03:14.218
I was reluctant to leave our current spot, which was protected by high cliffs.

51
00:03:14.999 --> 00:03:18.262
But my wife continued to make her argument for a house in the treetops.

52
00:03:18.842 --> 00:03:19.743
At last I agreed.

53
00:03:19.763 --> 00:03:25.448
"We'll have to build a bridge first," I said, "in order to carry everything across the stream."

54
00:03:26.524 --> 00:03:27.245
"A bridge!"

55
00:03:27.565 --> 00:03:28.205
she exclaimed.

56
00:03:28.225 --> 00:03:31.387
"I'll die from the heat if I have to wait for a bridge."

57
00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:35.530
"We'll need bags and baskets to carry everything," I said.

58
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.212
"If you focus on those, I promise the boys and I will make a bridge as quickly as

59
00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:46.036
possible." So the next day everyone set to work.

60
00:03:48.917 --> 00:03:52.720
Using planks that had washed up from the wreck, we soon completed our bridge.

61
00:03:54.284 --> 00:03:56.625
When moving day arrived, everyone was busy.

62
00:03:58.186 --> 00:03:59.347
Some collected provisions.

63
00:04:00.128 --> 00:04:04.750
Others packed kitchen utensils and tools into baskets tied onto the cow and donkey.

64
00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.832
We planned to return later for the ducks and geese.

65
00:04:09.653 --> 00:04:12.075
"Leave room for Franz to ride on the donkey!"

66
00:04:12.315 --> 00:04:13.175
my wife called out.

67
00:04:13.195 --> 00:04:16.818
"Oh! I almost forgot the chickens and pigeons!"

68
00:04:17.718 --> 00:04:20.240
Away ran the boys to catch the chickens and pigeons.

69
00:04:21.056 --> 00:04:24.939
The result was a lot of chasing, fluttering, cackling, and cooing.

70
00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.121
But they didn't catch any of them.

71
00:04:27.961 --> 00:04:30.503
At last my wife scattered some grain inside the tent.

72
00:04:32.485 --> 00:04:38.489
Lured by the food, the chickens and pigeons were easily caught, tied together, and placed on the cow's

73
00:04:38.549 --> 00:04:40.751
back. And off we went!

74
00:04:42.432 --> 00:04:44.173
Fritz and my wife led the caravan.

75
00:04:45.054 --> 00:04:47.896
Then came Franz on the donkey, followed by the cow.

76
00:04:48.704 --> 00:04:51.205
Jack led the goats with Knips riding one of them.

77
00:04:52.085 --> 00:04:53.546
Ernest was in charge of the sheep.

78
00:04:54.787 --> 00:04:57.528
I brought up the rear while the two dogs raced back and forth.

79
00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.671
Meanwhile the pig stubbornly refused to join us.

80
00:05:09.713 --> 00:05:14.195
We had just crossed the bridge when I heard the pig grunting and squealing angrily behind us.

81
00:05:15.035 --> 00:05:18.809
She had decided to come with us after all, but she clearly wasn't happy about it.
